// qwen-serve-run.bml — the resident serving loop: ONE long-lived fkwu process that owns the Qwen3.8-27B weights (Q8_0 and Q4_K_M, both when the memory governor allows) and the KV and serves every request from a spool.
//
//   echo '{"go":1}' | ./fkwu observe/qwen-serve-run.bml                       serve until a file named stop appears in the spool, finishing what runs
//   echo '{"go":1,"rows":8,"blocks":512,"dir":"/tmp/form-serve"}' | ./fkwu observe/qwen-serve-run.bml
//   echo '{"go":1,"models":["qwen38-q8"]}' | ./fkwu observe/qwen-serve-run.bml  one model, as the server always served
//   echo '{"prompt":"…","max_tokens":200}' | ./fkwu observe/serve-ask-run.bml      a client: request in, reply out (see that door)
//
// The techniques of vLLM, native in Form/BML/Metal (no vLLM here: it has no Metal backend). CONTINUOUS BATCHING: sequences join and leave between steps and ONE
// pass over the weights (q38m-step-core, the stream-row kernels of q38-multi.bml) advances every live sequence at once, so the weights are read once for
// all of them. PAGED KV: the K and V of every full-attention layer are one POOL of blocks (`blocks` of `block_positions` positions, default 512 of 256), a sequence's positions
// are blocks of it through a table row (q38pg-*, the paged kernels: the contiguous kernels' arithmetic with the address indirected, byte-identical), taken as the sequence advances and given back when it
// ends; the prefill lane writes into the pool through the same table. A row of the decode pass is only the sequence's recurrent state, so the sequences held at once are as many as the pool carries, up to `rows`.
// FLASH-DECODING: the split-KV attention serves every row. CHUNKED PREFILL: a new prompt is read 64 ids at a time on the prefill lane, one chunk a tick when the scheduler says it is due, its recurrent state then copied into its
// row, so a long prompt does not stall the streams that decode (form-stdlib/bml/serve-sched.bml; its band needs no model). The PREFIX CACHE keeps blocks too: an entry is copies of a prefix's blocks and
// its recurrent state, taken from the same pool and let go, least recently used first, when the pool or the machine is short.
//
// MORE THAN ONE MODEL, ONE PROCESS, ONE GPU LEASE. `models` names the registry voices to hold (default qwen38-q8 alone: Q4_K_M answers nothing readable through this server today and decodes slower, so it is named only to measure it; the first is never refused, a later one is skipped by name when the memory governor holds it). Each
// model's file is mapped once (the governor is asked once per model, and a lease of the same file is shared), and each has its own context, block pool (`blocks` for the first, `side_blocks` for the others, default 128),
// prefix cache, scheduler state and standing limit; the weights are the only thing the models share with the machine. A request names its model (`model`), else the registry's first loaded voice for the role its `who`
// names (serve-sched.bml svs-role-of; model-registry.bml mr-chain-names: guide, lens, counsel, triage -> the quarter-size file, plan, candidate, diagnose -> Q8_0); a model that is not held is a named refusal, never a hang.
// The tick loop runs one model's tick at a time, the model with the least recent GPU time that has work (consumed ms, decayed with a half-life of about 8 s): a long prefill on one model never holds a short ask on the other
// beyond one tick, and no fixed cap truncates anything.
//
// The spool (default /tmp/form-serve, one for the machine as the GPU lease is): req/<id>.json one request a file (a client writes tmp/ then renames); the server
// claims it into work/, writes reply/<id>.json (whole or absent) and one row of ledger.jsonl: id, model, who, status, prompt_ids, generated_ids, wall_ms, queue_ms,
// prefill_ms, decode_ms, decode_tok_s, surprise_micro_nats, slot, rent_tokens 0. status.json names the server (pid, start) for the clients; a file named
// stop ends it after what runs is finished; a file named limit holds a standing limit on sequences admitted at once (for each model).
//
// PRESSURE SLOWS OR YIELDS, NEVER TRUNCATES. The memory governor's reading (memory-governor.bml mg-sense) sets how many blocks a pool may have in use while others run
// (svs-budget): a prompt waits in the queue when the pool or the budget cannot give its blocks, goes in when others free them, and the cache's least recently used entries go first;
// a sequence that finds the pool empty yields its blocks and is read again later, never cut, and a sequence alone is never held. A reply ends at the model's end of turn, at a stop
// string or a count its request named; a prompt or a sequence that alone outgrows the pool is named pool-too-small or pool-full, with the numbers.
// The server holds the GPU lease for its whole life with an owner line that names it (gpu-lease-door-hold: every turn inside inherits it); other tenants wait. The
// live ear skips its whisper pass while .hearth/ear.yield stands and the lease is held, so this door writes that flag while it serves (yield_ear 1, the default).
//
// stdin, one JSON line, strict: go (1 to serve; without it only the plan is said), dir, models (registry names), rows (1..8, default 8: the rows of each model's decode pass), blocks (the first model's pool, default 512; fewer when the
// attention scratch cannot hold the partials of that many positions), side_blocks (each later model's pool, default 128), block_positions (a power of two, default 256), maxpos (positions the attention scratch is opened for, default 65536),
// chunk (prompt ids a prefill chunk, default and most 64), share (the percent of the decoders' wall time a prefill may take while they decode, default 50), span (positions the prefill scratch holds, default 64, up to 512), idle_chunk (ids a chunk
// reads when nothing decodes, default span), poll_ms (the nap when nothing runs, default 20), idle_exit_ms (end after this long idle; 0 never, default 0), yield_ear (0 or 1, default 1), reserve_gib (what the machine keeps for others,
// default 8), limit (a standing limit on sequences admitted at once, 0 none), spec (columns one weight pass may carry: 0 or 1 none, 2 to 8 default 8), spec_floor, spec_nmin (see SPECULATION).
// Greedy decoding and temperature draws; an envelope or a grammar in a request is refused by name (the caller runs its own session for one). A physical run: it needs the local GPU.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/line-grammar.fk form-stdlib/json.fk form-stdlib/bml/stdin-source.bml form-stdlib/bml/door-options.bml form-stdlib/bml/q38-multi.bml form-stdlib/bml/q38-verify.bml form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-code-live.bml form-stdlib/bml/q38-lenses.bml form-stdlib/bml/memory-governor.bml form-stdlib/bml/serve-sched.bml form-stdlib/bml/flow-signal.bml form-stdlib/spool-bell-transport.fk native/metal/qwen35-dense-token-handle.fk native/metal/qwen35-dense-spec.fk form-stdlib/bml/ledger.bml form-stdlib/bml/host-fs.bml form-stdlib/bml/coordination.bml form-stdlib/query-lane-resolve.bml form-stdlib/qwen35-artifact-seal-reader.fk form-stdlib/bml/local-run.bml form-stdlib/model-registry.bml
section [form.bml] {
 // the server's own state: the spill of prefill states (ids are unique across models), the signal frame and bell, the counts, the leases
 let SV = record_new(0, "pre", [], "flow", nothing(), "bell", nothing(), "served", 0, "tokens", 0, "yield", 0, "dir", "", "lease", []);
 class QwenServeRun {
  def qsr-say(t) = print_str("[serve] " ++ t ++ "\n");
  def qsr-spec() = [["go", "int"], ["dir", "str"], ["rows", "int"], ["blocks", "int"], ["block_positions", "int"], ["maxpos", "int"], ["chunk", "int"], ["share", "int"], ["poll_ms", "int"], ["idle_exit_ms", "int"], ["yield_ear", "int"], ["reserve_gib", "int"], ["limit", "int"], ["span", "int"], ["idle_chunk", "int"], ["spec", "int"], ["spec_floor", "int"], ["spec_nmin", "int"], ["models", "strs"], ["side_blocks", "int"]];
  // what each model keeps of its own: its prefix cache, its limit and pressure readings, its beat and its share of the GPU
  def qsr-mstate() = record_new(0, "cache", [], "serial", 0, "evict_at", 0, "cache_hits", 0, "cache_ids", 0, "limit", 1, "limit_at", 0, "budget", -1, "budget_at", 0, "beat_at", 0, "beat_say", 0, "beat_key", "", "shed_at", 0, "step_ms", 0, "steps", 0, "ticks", 0, "gpu_ms", 0, "gpu_at", 0);
  // SPECULATION (q38-verify.bml, serve-sched.bml): spec is the columns one weight pass may carry (0 or 1: none; 2 to 8, default 8, at most the rows). A greedy row that finds in its own text what followed the last time its last few ids
  // occurred carries that as drafts, and the pass verifies them (the exact association's arithmetic: every column carries the bits of a one-token decode), accepting the longest run the model repeats and one
  // more id: the same reply, byte for byte, as one id a pass, sooner. A column costs every live row of the pass a part of a token, so a draft takes one only when its likelihood of standing
  // is above spec_floor per mille of a token for each row that waits on the pass (default 300); spec_nmin is the shortest suffix a lookup may match (default 2).
  def qsr-spec-width(o, rows) = qsr-clamp(qsr-int(o, "spec", 8), 0, rows > 8 ? 8 : rows);
  def qsr-span(o) = qsr-clamp(qsr-int(o, "span", 64), 64, 512);
  def qsr-int(o, key, d) = json-object-has?(o, key) ? json-int-value(json-object-get(o, key)) : d;
  def qsr-str(o, key, d) = json-object-has?(o, key) ? json-string-value(json-object-get(o, key)) : d;
  def qsr-clamp(x, lo, hi) = x < lo ? lo : x > hi ? hi : x;
  def qsr-suffix?(name, suffix) = len(name) > len(suffix) && substring(name, len(name) - len(suffix), len(name)) == suffix;
  def qsr-dirs(dir) = host_dir_mkdir(dir) + host_dir_mkdir(dir ++ "/tmp") + host_dir_mkdir(dir ++ "/req") + host_dir_mkdir(dir ++ "/work") + host_dir_mkdir(dir ++ "/reply");
  // a file is written whole or not at all: staged under tmp/, then renamed
  def qsr-put(dir, path, text) {
   let stage = dir ++ "/tmp/" ++ host_pid().str() ++ "-" ++ now_unix_ms().str() ++ ".stage";
   let w = write_file(stage, text);
   w < 0 ? -1 : host_path_rename(stage, path);
  }
  def qsr-append(path, text) = sbt-append-count(path, text);
  // the block's log2 (positions a block holds are a power of two: the kernels read p >> bsh and p & (2^bsh - 1))
  def qsr-log2(n) = n <= 1 ? 0 : 1 + qsr-log2(n / 2);
  def qsr-list(xs) = tb-join(xs, x => x, ",");
  def qsr-names(o) {
   let n = svs-strs(o, "models");
   len(n) > 0 ? n : ["qwen38-q8"];
  }
  def qsr-run() {
   let o = dop-doc("qwen-serve", stdin-text(), qsr-spec());
   let dir = qsr-str(o, "dir", "/tmp/form-serve");
   let rows = qsr-clamp(qsr-int(o, "rows", 8), 1, 8);
   let maxpos = qsr-clamp(qsr-int(o, "maxpos", 65536), 256, 1048576);
   let bsh = qsr-clamp(qsr-log2(qsr-int(o, "block_positions", 256)), 0, 8);
   let blocks = qsr-clamp(qsr-int(o, "blocks", 512), 2, 1000000);
   qsr-int(o, "go", 0) != 1 ? qsr-say("plan: go=1 serves " ++ qsr-list(qsr-names(o)) ++ ", up to " ++ rows.str() ++ " rows each, a pool of " ++ blocks.str() ++ " blocks of " ++ q38pg-bsz(bsh).str() ++ " positions for the first (attention scratch for " ++ maxpos.str() ++ ") from the spool " ++ dir ++ " until a file named stop appears there") : qsr-held(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks, bsh);
  }
  def qsr-held(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks, bsh) {
   let made = qsr-dirs(dir);
   let st = qsr-standing-at(dir);
   (String) st[0] == "standing" ? qsr-say("a server already stands for " ++ dir ++ " (pid " ++ json-int-value(json-object-get(st[1], "pid")).str() ++ "); this one does not start") : qsr-asked(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks, bsh);
  }
  // The memory governor is asked first, before the GPU lease or a byte of a model is mapped, once per model: the weights (charged once with any live lease of the same file, so a second open of the
  // same model is shared mapping, not a copy) and reserve_gib kept free. The first model's refusal is the governor's line and the door's exit; a later model that is held is skipped by name.
  // A grant is a lease the server holds while it stands. Answers [name, path, lease] for each model granted.
  def qsr-asked(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks, bsh) {
   let got = foldl((acc, name) => qsr-grant(o, acc, name), [], qsr-names(o));
   let kept = record_set(SV, "lease", map(g => g[2], got));
   gpu-lease-door-hold("qwen-serve resident server pid " ++ host_pid().str() ++ " spool " ++ dir ++ " models " ++ qsr-list(map(g => g[0], got)) ++ " rows " ++ rows.str() ++ " pool " ++ blocks.str() ++ " blocks of " ++ q38pg-bsz(bsh).str(), () => qsr-serve(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks, bsh, got));
  }
  def qsr-grant(o, acc, name) {
   let path = mr-path(mr-find(name));
   let wbytes = len(path) == 0 ? -1 : file_size(path);
   wbytes <= 0 ? (nil?(acc) ? dop-refuse("qwen-serve", "the model " ++ name ++ " has no file here (" ++ path ++ ")") : qsr-skipped(acc, name, "no file")) : qsr-grant-ask(o, acc, name, path, wbytes);
  }
  def qsr-grant-ask(o, acc, name, path, wbytes) {
   let v = mg-door-first("qwen-serve resident server " ++ name, path, wbytes, 0, qsr-int(o, "reserve_gib", 8) * 1073741824);
   !mg-granted?(v) ? (nil?(acc) ? dop-refuse("qwen-serve", mg-held-reason() ++ v[1] ++ "; refused before the GPU lease or any mapping") : qsr-skipped(acc, name, v[1])) : append(acc, [[name, path, mg-reservation-of(mg-lease("qwen-serve resident server pid " ++ host_pid().str() ++ " " ++ name, path, wbytes, 0))]]);
  }
  def qsr-skipped(acc, name, why) {
   let a = qsr-say("model " ++ name ++ " is not held: " ++ why);
   acc;
  }
  def qsr-standing-at(dir) {
   let t = read_file(dir ++ "/status.json");
   nothing?(t) || len(trim(t)) == 0 ? ["absent", "no status"] : qsr-standing-doc(try parse-json("serve-status", trim(t)) catch nothing());
  }
  def qsr-standing-doc(doc) {
   let row = nothing?(doc) ? nothing() : host_process(json-int-value(json-object-get(doc, "pid")));
   (String) value_kind(row) == "list" && row[5] == json-int-value(json-object-get(doc, "start")) && json-int-value(json-object-get(doc, "pid")) != host_pid() ? ["standing", doc] : ["absent", "no live server"];
  }
  // ── the models, the lanes and the loop ──
  // a model is [c, env]: c its context (the lists below), env the scheduler's functions over it
  def qsr-serve(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks, bsh, got) {
   let start = host_process(host_pid())[5];
   let label = "qwen-serve pid " ++ host_pid().str();
   let w0 = qsr-status(dir, "opening", start, label, svs-new(rows), nothing());
   let yielded = qsr-yield-on(qsr-int(o, "yield_ear", 1));
   let t0 = host_monotonic_ms();
   // the kernels every model shares (they carry no model's geometry)
   let shared = [q38s-pipes(q38s-msl()), q38m-pipes(q38m-msl()), q38pg-pipes()];
   let ms = foldl((acc, i) => qsr-mount-one(o, dir, rows, maxpos, i == 0 ? blocks : qsr-int(o, "side_blocks", 128), bsh, start, label, yielded, shared, got[i], acc), [], range(0, len(got)));
   let acked = len(ms) == 0 ? 0 : qsr-lease-ack();
   len(ms) == 0 ? qsr-ended(dir, yielded, "the model did not open (file " ++ got[0][1] ++ ")") : qsr-up(o, dir, rows, start, label, yielded, t0, ms);
  }
  def qsr-mount-one(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks0, bsh, start, label, yielded, shared, g, acc) {
   let t0 = host_monotonic_ms();
   let ctx = q38-open-span(g[1], maxpos, qsr-span(o));
   len(ctx) == 0 ? qsr-opened-not(acc, g) : append(acc, [qsr-mount(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks0, bsh, start, label, yielded, shared, g, ctx, t0)]);
  }
  def qsr-opened-not(acc, g) {
   let a = qsr-say("model " ++ g[0] ++ " did not open (file " ++ g[1] ++ ")");
   acc;
  }
  // The pool holds as many blocks as were asked unless the attention scratch cannot hold the partials of that many positions (q38sp-fits?): the split kernels write nspl partials a row, nspl the
  // longest sequence's positions over 256, and the scratch was opened for `maxpos`; the pool is then the blocks that fit, and the door says so (a larger maxpos opens a larger scratch).
  def qsr-fit-blocks(geo, bsh, blocks) = blocks <= 2 ? blocks : q38sp-fits?(geo[12], geo[13], geo[14], geo[18], q38sp-nspl(blocks * q38pg-bsz(bsh), 0)) ? blocks : qsr-fit-blocks(geo, bsh, (blocks * 15) / 16);
  def qsr-mount(o, dir, rows, maxpos, blocks0, bsh, start, label, yielded, shared, g, ctx, t0) {
   let geo = ctx[2];
   let blocks = qsr-fit-blocks(geo, bsh, blocks0);
   let sx = q38s-open(ctx, 8, 8);
   let posb = metal_buf_alloc(64);
   let lpb = metal_buf_alloc(64);
   let spb = metal_buf_alloc(256);
   // one table row a decode row and one a prefill state (row `rows` + the sequence's slot: any number of prompts are read at once), a sequence able to hold every block
   let tstride = blocks;
   let tbl = metal_buf_alloc(2 * rows * tstride * 4);
   let page = q38pg-page(tbl, bsh, tstride, 0, shared[2], shared[1], ctx[0][q38sp-index() + 3]);
   let arena = q38pg-new-arena(geo, rows, blocks, bsh, page, bytes => metal_buf_alloc(bytes));
   let pool = svb-new(blocks, q38pg-bsz(bsh));
   let eos = qsx-load(ctx[9])[2];
   // the verify pass's own kernels (the segment recurrences) and its segment table, only when the server speculates: a server that does not runs exactly the pass it always ran
   let vk = qsr-spec-width(o, rows) >= 2 ? q38v-open(q38v-msl()) : 0;
   let c = [ctx, shared[0], shared[1], arena, sx, posb, lpb, dir, eos, rows, o, start, label, yielded, spb, pool, shared[2], tbl, tstride, bsh, page, vk, qsr-mstate(), g[0], g[1]];
   let a = qsr-say(g[0] ++ " opened in " ++ (host_monotonic_ms() - t0).str() ++ " ms: " ++ rows.str() ++ " rows, a pool of " ++ blocks.str() ++ " blocks of " ++ q38pg-bsz(bsh).str() ++ " positions (" ++ (blocks * q38pg-bsz(bsh)).str() ++ " in all" ++ (blocks < blocks0 ? ", fewer than the " ++ blocks0.str() ++ " asked: the attention scratch of " ++ maxpos.str() ++ " positions holds no more partials" : "") ++ "), " ++ (qsr-block-bytes(c) / 1048576).str() ++ " MiB a block, end-of-turn id " ++ eos.str());
   [c, qsr-env(c)];
  }
  def qsr-up(o, dir, rows, start, label, yielded, t0, ms) {
   let names = map(m => m[0][23], ms);
   let w = qsr-status(dir, "standing " ++ qsr-list(names), start, label, svs-new(rows), ms[0][0][15]);
   let fl = record_set(SV, "flow", fsg-new(15, "serve"));
   let dr = record_set(SV, "dir", dir);
   let bl = record_set(SV, "bell", fsg-open-handle("/fgn-serve-bell"));
   let up = qsr-sig("ok", rows, svb-capacity(ms[0][0][15]), "standing", "pid=" ++ host_pid().str(), host_monotonic_ms() - t0);
   let why = qsr-loop(ms, map(m => svs-new(rows), ms), 0);
   let freed = foldl((n, m) => n + qsr-unmount(m[0]), 0, ms) + qsr-pre-free-all();
   qsr-ended(dir, yielded, why);
  }
  def qsr-unmount(c) = qsr-cache-free(c) + q38-free-state(c[3]) + q38s-close(c[4]) + q38-free-handle(c[5]) + q38-free-handle(c[6]) + q38-free-handle(c[14]) + q38-free-handle(c[17]) + (c[21] == 0 ? 0 : q38v-close(c[21])) + qlz-close(c[0]);
  // the bytes of one block over every full layer's K and V
  def qsr-block-bytes(c) = q38pg-bsz(c[19]) * c[0][2][20] * 4 * 2 * q38-full-layers(c[0][2][21], c[0][2][22]);
  // the weights show in the machine's own reading once mapped: the leases' shared promises are then observed, and they go back when the server ends
  def qsr-lease-ack() = foldl((n, l) => n + (record?(l) ? mg-reservation-ack-shared(l) : 0), 0, record_get(SV, "lease"));
  def qsr-lease-release() = foldl((n, l) => n + (record?(l) ? mg-reservation-release(l) : 0), 0, record_get(SV, "lease"));
  def qsr-ended(dir, yielded, why) {
   let a = qsr-say("ended: " ++ why ++ "; served " ++ record_get(SV, "served").str() ++ " requests, " ++ record_get(SV, "tokens").str() ++ " tokens");
   let sg = qsr-sig("end", record_get(SV, "served"), 0, "ended", "tokens=" ++ record_get(SV, "tokens").str(), 0);
   let b = host_path_remove(dir ++ "/status.json");
   let d = host_path_remove(dir ++ "/stop");
   let y = yielded == 1 ? host_path_remove(".hearth/ear.yield") : 0;
   let l = qsr-lease-release();
   0;
  }
  // the live ear stands down while this server holds the lease and the flag stands; the door writes the flag if it was absent and takes it away at the end
  def qsr-yield-on(want) {
   let h = host_dir_mkdir(".hearth");
   want == 1 && file_size(".hearth/ear.yield") < 0 ? { let w = write_file(".hearth/ear.yield", "qwen-serve pid " ++ host_pid().str() ++ " holds the GPU lease\n"); 1; } : 0;
  }
  // ── the functions the scheduler is given ──
  def qsr-env(c) = [() => host_monotonic_ms(), () => qsr-limit(c), s => qsr-begin(c, s), (s, ids, pos) => qsr-chunk(c, s, ids, pos), s => qsr-fork(c, s), rows => qsr-decode(c, rows), s => qsr-stop-hit(c, s), c[15], tok => tok == c[8], qsr-clamp(qsr-int(c[10], "chunk", 64), 1, qsr-span(c[10])), qsr-clamp(qsr-int(c[10], "share", 50), 1, 10000), (s, count) => qsr-snap(c, s, count), () => qsr-budget(c), need => qsr-reclaim(c, need), qsr-clamp(qsr-int(c[10], "idle_chunk", qsr-span(c[10])), 1, qsr-span(c[10])), rows => qsr-verify(c, rows), qsr-spec-width(c[10], c[9]), qsr-clamp(qsr-int(c[10], "spec_floor", 300), 0, 1000), qsr-clamp(qsr-int(c[10], "spec_nmin", 2), 1, 3)];
  // ── the prefix cache (each model's own: c[22] is its state) ──
  // A prompt read once is read once: the prefill lane's state after a prefix of ids is kept (a snapshot: the full layers' K and V to that position, as BLOCKS taken from the pool, and the linear layers' state),
  // and a later request whose ids begin with the same prefix starts from a copy of it and reads only what follows. Where a snapshot is taken: at every prompt's end (a session's next
  // turn continues it), at the boundary between a counsel's question and a lens's own text (N lenses read the question once), and at 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192 ... ids. An entry is [the ids packed four bytes each, how many, the linear state,
  // the last use, the serial, the blocks]; it is compared by those bytes, never assumed. An entry costs the blocks of the positions it holds. PRESSURE YIELDS: when the pool has too few blocks for a prompt or a sequence's next
  // position, or the machine's available bytes fall under a few blocks plus the reserve, the least recently used entry is released (qsr-release-lru), one at a time, until the pressure is gone or none is left; no count caps the cache.
  def qsr-key(packed, n) = substring(packed, 0, 4 * n);
  def qsr-entry-match?(e, packed, most) = e[1] <= most && qsr-key(packed, e[1]) == e[0];
  def qsr-cache-best(M, packed, most) = foldl((best, e) => qsr-entry-match?(e, packed, most) && (nothing?(best) || e[1] > best[1]) ? e : best, nothing(), record_get(M, "cache"));
  def qsr-cache-has?(M, packed, n) = any?(e => e[1] == n && e[0] == qsr-key(packed, n), record_get(M, "cache"));
  // an entry is told by its serial (e[4]), never by comparing states
  def qsr-cache-touch(M, e) = record_set(M, "cache", map(x => x[4] == e[4] ? [x[0], x[1], x[2], host_monotonic_ms(), x[4], x[5]] : x, record_get(M, "cache")));
  def qsr-cache-add(M, packed, n, lin, blocks) {
   let serial = record_get(M, "serial") + 1;
   let a = record_set(M, "serial", serial);
   record_set(M, "cache", append(record_get(M, "cache"), [[qsr-key(packed, n), n, lin, host_monotonic_ms(), serial, blocks]]));
  }
  // the recurrent state alone is what a state's linear layers hold: the buffers of a prefill state or an entry (the full layers' K and V are the pool's, never freed here)
  def qsr-free-sts(sts) = foldl((n, row) => n + q38-free-handle(row[0]) + q38-free-handle(row[1]), 0, sts);
  // positions [0, n) of the blocks src copied into the blocks dst (block j of one to block j of the other, the last one's first n - j * bsz positions), every full layer's K and V
  def qsr-copy-blocks(c, src, dst, n) {
   let bsz = q38pg-bsz(c[19]);
   foldl((a, j) => a + q38pg-copy-block(c[16], c[0][2], c[3], c[19], src[j], dst[j], n - j * bsz > bsz ? bsz : n - j * bsz), 0, range(0, svb-blocks-for(bsz, n)));
  }
  // an entry restored into a sequence's blocks and recurrent state, or the sequence's into an entry's
  def qsr-restore(c, e, blocks, sts) = gpu-lease-turn("qwen serve prefix hit", () => {
   let batch = metal_batch_concurrent();
   let lin = q38pg-copy-linear(c[2][5], c[0][2], e[2], sts, 0, 0);
   let moved = qsr-copy-blocks(c, e[5], blocks, e[1]);
   metal_sync();
  });
  // Every sequence being read has a prefill state of its own and a table row of its own (row `rows` + its slot), kept in SV "pre" as [id, the state, the ids packed] until it is forked, shed or the server ends.
  def qsr-pre-of(id) = foldl((f, e) => (String) e[0] == (String) id ? e : f, nothing(), record_get(SV, "pre"));
  def qsr-pre-sts(id) = qsr-pre-of(id)[1];
  def qsr-pre-packed(id) = qsr-pre-of(id)[2];
  def qsr-pre-set(id, sts, packed) = record_set(SV, "pre", append(filter(e => (String) e[0] != (String) id, record_get(SV, "pre")), [[id, sts, packed]]));
  def qsr-pre-drop(id) = record_set(SV, "pre", filter(e => (String) e[0] != (String) id, record_get(SV, "pre")));
  // a state that never forked (its sequence was shed) goes back: its recurrent buffers are freed and its entry dropped; the blocks were given back by the scheduler
  def qsr-pre-free(id) {
   let e = qsr-pre-of(id);
   let n = nothing?(e) ? 0 : qsr-free-sts(e[1]);
   let d = qsr-pre-drop(id);
   n;
  }
  def qsr-pre-free-all() = foldl((n, e) => n + qsr-free-sts(e[1]), 0, record_get(SV, "pre"));
  // the prefill lane opens a state for a sequence: its table row written (the prefill row), a copy of the longest cached prefix of its ids (at most all but the last, which is the first decode row's input),
  // else a fresh one. Answers how many ids the state already holds.
  def qsr-begin(c, s) {
   let sts = q38pg-new-state(c[0][2], c[3], (c[9] + s[7]) * c[18], bytes => metal_buf_alloc(bytes));
   let packed = q38m-uints(s[3]);
   let a = qsr-pre-set(s[0], sts, packed);
   let w = q38pg-write-table(c[17], c[18], c[9] + s[7], s[24]);
   let hit = qsr-cache-best(c[22], packed, len(s[3]) - 1);
   nothing?(hit) ? 0 : qsr-hit(c, s, hit, sts);
  }
  def qsr-hit(c, s, hit, sts) {
   let moved = qsr-restore(c, hit, s[24], sts);
   let a = qsr-cache-touch(c[22], hit);
   let b = record_set(c[22], "cache_hits", record_get(c[22], "cache_hits") + 1);
   let d = record_set(c[22], "cache_ids", record_get(c[22], "cache_ids") + hit[1]);
   let said = qsr-say("prefix cache (" ++ c[23] ++ "): " ++ s[0] ++ " starts from " ++ hit[1].str() ++ " of its " ++ len(s[3]).str() ++ " ids");
   hit[1];
  }
  // the lane has read `count` ids: keep the state as it stands unless an entry for exactly this prefix exists or the pool (the cache's own least recently used entries let go first) and the machine have
  // no blocks to spare for it (a snapshot is a convenience, never taken from a sequence)
  def qsr-snap(c, s, count) {
   let packed = qsr-pre-packed(s[0]);
   qsr-cache-has?(c[22], packed, count) ? 0 : qsr-snap-room(c, s, packed, count, svb-blocks-for(q38pg-bsz(c[19]), count));
  }
  def qsr-snap-room(c, s, packed, count, k) {
   let have = svb-free-n(c[15]) >= k ? svb-free-n(c[15]) : qsr-reclaim(c, k);
   let b = qsr-budget(c);
   have < k || (b >= 0 && svb-used(c[15]) + k > b) ? 0 : qsr-snap-keep(c, s, packed, count, k);
  }
  def qsr-snap-keep(c, s, packed, count, k) {
   let blocks = svb-take(c[15], k);
   let lin = q38pg-new-linear(c[0][2], bytes => metal_buf_alloc(bytes));
   let moved = gpu-lease-turn("qwen serve snapshot", () => {
    let batch = metal_batch_concurrent();
    let l = q38pg-copy-linear(c[2][5], c[0][2], qsr-pre-sts(s[0]), lin, 0, 0);
    let m = qsr-copy-blocks(c, s[24], blocks, count);
    metal_sync();
   });
   qsr-cache-add(c[22], packed, count, lin, blocks);
   count;
  }
  // the least recently used entry is released when the machine's available bytes fall under a few blocks plus the reserve (one entry a reading, read at most every 2 s)
  def qsr-evict(c) = host_monotonic_ms() - record_get(c[22], "evict_at") < 2000 || nil?(record_get(c[22], "cache")) ? 0 : qsr-evict-read(c);
  def qsr-evict-read(c) {
   let a = record_set(c[22], "evict_at", host_monotonic_ms());
   let vm = mg-sense();
   let avail = mg-vm-ok?(vm) ? mg-available(vm) : -1;
   avail >= 0 && avail < 4 * qsr-block-bytes(c) + qsr-int(c[10], "reserve_gib", 8) * 1073741824 ? qsr-release-lru(c, "pressure: " ++ mg-gib-text(avail) ++ " available") : 0;
  }
  def qsr-release-lru(c, why) {
   let rows = record_get(c[22], "cache");
   let old = foldl((o, e) => e[3] < o[3] ? e : o, rows[0], rows);
   let a = record_set(c[22], "cache", filter(e => e[4] != old[4], rows));
   let b = svb-release(c[15], old[5]);
   let f = qsr-free-sts(old[2]);
   qsr-say("released the prefix cache's entry of " ++ old[1].str() ++ " ids (" ++ c[23] ++ ", " ++ why ++ ")");
  }
  // blocks free for `need` taken by letting entries go, least recently used first; answers the blocks free
  def qsr-reclaim(c, need) = svb-free-n(c[15]) >= need || nil?(record_get(c[22], "cache")) ? svb-free-n(c[15]) : qsr-reclaim-more(c, need);
  def qsr-reclaim-more(c, need) {
   let r = qsr-release-lru(c, "the pool is short of " ++ need.str() ++ " blocks");
   qsr-reclaim(c, need);
  }
  def qsr-cache-free(c) = foldl((n, e) => n + qsr-free-sts(e[2]), 0, record_get(c[22], "cache"));
  // the prompt's own end is kept too: the blocks of its positions gain the entry as an owner (no copy; positions past the prompt are the sequence's own and the entry never reads them), its recurrent
  // state is the entry's (the prefill state itself, a copy went into the row)
  def qsr-adopt(c, s, sts) {
   let packed = qsr-pre-packed(s[0]);
   qsr-cache-has?(c[22], packed, s[8]) ? qsr-free-sts(sts) : qsr-adopt-keep(c, s, packed, sts);
  }
  def qsr-adopt-keep(c, s, packed, sts) {
   let blocks = take(svb-blocks-for(q38pg-bsz(c[19]), s[8]), s[24]);
   let a = svb-retain(c[15], blocks);
   qsr-cache-add(c[22], packed, s[8], sts, blocks);
  }
  // A chunk is waited for before the scheduler reads the clock: submitted and left in flight, its GPU time was billed to the decode step that followed, so the share governor (prefill ms against decode ms)
  // saw no prefill time and ran a chunk every tick. Read at its true cost, a prefill takes the share it was given.
  def qsr-chunk(c, s, ids, pos) {
   let r = q38-prefill-span-batched(c[0][0], c[0][1], c[0][2], c[0][3], qsr-pre-sts(s[0]), c[0][4], c[0][5], c[0][6], ids, pos);
   let w = metal_sync();
   r;
  }
  // the prefill state's recurrent state is copied into the sequence's row of the arena (its K and V are already the pool's blocks); the state is adopted by the prefix cache or goes back
  def qsr-fork(c, s) {
   let sts = qsr-pre-sts(s[0]);
   let done = gpu-lease-turn("qwen serve fork", () => {
    let batch = metal_batch_concurrent();
    let moved = q38pg-copy-linear(c[2][5], c[0][2], sts, c[3], s[7], 0);
    metal_sync();
   });
   let freed = qsr-adopt(c, s, sts);
   qsr-pre-drop(s[0]);
  }
  // one pass over the weights for every row; answers [greedy id, surprise in micro-nats] a row. Each row's table row is written first: its sequence's blocks, or the sink's for a free row.
  def qsr-decode(c, rows) {
   let t0 = host_monotonic_ms();
   let tw = foldl((a, x) => a + qsr-table-row(c, x), 0, rows);
   // a row that names a temperature draws its token (q38m-sample-msl); every other row keeps the greedy id, and a pass of greedy rows runs no draw kernel at all
   let sampled = any?(x => x[3] > 0, rows);
   let r = sampled ? q38m-step-draw(c[0], c[1], c[2], c[3], c[4], c[5], map(x => x[1], rows), map(x => x[2], rows), c[6], c[14], map(x => [x[3], x[3] > 0 ? q38m-sample-key(x[4], x[5]) : 0], rows)) : q38m-step-core(c[0], c[1], c[2], c[3], c[4], c[5], map(x => x[1], rows), map(x => x[2], rows), c[6]);
   let a = record_set(c[22], "step_ms", record_get(c[22], "step_ms") + (host_monotonic_ms() - t0));
   let b = record_set(c[22], "steps", record_get(c[22], "steps") + 1);
   map(i => [r[0][i], r[1][i]], range(0, len(rows)));
  }
  // one pass over the weights for every live row with the drafts some carry (q38v-pass): a row of the scheduler is [slot, pending id, position, temperature, seed, tokens said, blocks, drafts]; the pass lays out its
  // columns row after row (a table row each, the row's blocks written into it: the rows below `rows` the decode pass uses, so the prefill lane's rows are never touched) and answers a list a row
  // [the ids accepted, their surprises, drafts accepted, drafts tried]; a row whose drafts fell was put back to the recurrent state after its last accepted id.
  def qsr-verify(c, rows) {
   let t0 = host_monotonic_ms();
   let r = q38v-pass([c[0], c[1], c[2], c[21], c[3], c[4], c[5], c[6], c[14], c[17], c[18], c[16]], map(x => [x[0], x[1], x[2], x[6], x[7], x[3], x[3] > 0 ? q38m-sample-key(x[4], x[5]) : 0, 0], rows));
   let a = record_set(c[22], "step_ms", record_get(c[22], "step_ms") + (host_monotonic_ms() - t0));
   let b = record_set(c[22], "steps", record_get(c[22], "steps") + 1);
   r;
  }
  def qsr-table-row(c, x) {
   let w = q38pg-write-table(c[17], c[18], x[0], nil?(x[6]) ? [0] : x[6]);
   1;
  }
  // a stop string the request named, looked for in the tail of what the sequence said
  // (a token is at least one byte of text, so a stop string of n bytes lies within the last n ids: the tail looked at is the longest stop's length, and at least 24 ids)
  def qsr-stop-hit(c, s) = nil?(s[5]) ? false : qsr-has-any?(qlz-detok(c[0], reverse(take(foldl((a, st) => len(st) > a ? len(st) : a, 24, s[5]), s[9]))), s[5]);
  def qsr-has-any?(text, stops) = any?(st => len(st) > 0 && str_find(text, st, 0) >= 0, stops);
  // the standing limit on sequences admitted at once (the `limit` option or file; 0 none), read at most every 2 s
  def qsr-limit(c) = host_monotonic_ms() - record_get(c[22], "limit_at") < 2000 ? record_get(c[22], "limit") : qsr-limit-read(c);
  def qsr-limit-read(c) {
   let ctlf = read_file(c[7] ++ "/limit");
   let ctl = nothing?(ctlf) ? 0 : (str_to_int(trim(ctlf)) ?? 0);
   let n = svs-limit(c[9], qsr-pick-ctl(qsr-int(c[10], "limit", 0), ctl));
   let said = n != record_get(c[22], "limit") ? qsr-say("standing limit (" ++ c[23] ++ "): admitting " ++ n.str() ++ " of " ++ c[9].str() ++ " rows at once") : 0;
   let a = record_set(c[22], "limit", n);
   let b = record_set(c[22], "limit_at", host_monotonic_ms());
   n;
  }
  def qsr-pick-ctl(a, b) = a > 0 && (b <= 0 || a < b) ? a : b > 0 ? b : 0;
  // the machine's pressure on the pool: how many blocks may be in use while others run (svs-budget; negative none claimed), read at most every 2 s, said when it changes
  def qsr-budget(c) = host_monotonic_ms() - record_get(c[22], "budget_at") < 2000 ? record_get(c[22], "budget") : qsr-budget-read(c);
  def qsr-budget-read(c) {
   let vm = mg-sense();
   let avail = mg-vm-ok?(vm) ? mg-available(vm) : -1;
   let b = svs-budget(svb-used(c[15]), avail, qsr-block-bytes(c), qsr-int(c[10], "reserve_gib", 8) * 1073741824);
   let said = b != record_get(c[22], "budget") && b >= 0 && svb-used(c[15]) + 1 > b ? qsr-say("pressure (" ++ c[23] ++ "): the pool may have " ++ b.str() ++ " of its " ++ svb-capacity(c[15]).str() ++ " blocks in use (" ++ mg-gib-text(avail < 0 ? 0 : avail) ++ " available): a new prompt waits") : 0;
   let a = record_set(c[22], "budget", b);
   let d = record_set(c[22], "budget_at", host_monotonic_ms());
   b;
  }
  // ── the loop ──
  // ms: the models [c, env]; Ss: the scheduler state of each. Each pass: claim and route the requests that arrived, shed the dead clients' sequences, run ONE tick of the model with the least recent GPU time
  // that has work, write what finished, keep the beat. Answers why it ended.
  def qsr-loop(ms, Ss, idle_since) {
   let dir = ms[0][0][7];
   let stopping = file_size(dir ++ "/stop") >= 0;
   let S1 = stopping ? Ss : qsr-shed-all(ms, qsr-intake(ms, Ss));
   let i = qsr-pick(ms, S1);
   i < 0 ? qsr-quiet(ms, S1, stopping, idle_since) : qsr-tick(ms, S1, i);
  }
  // consumed ms, decayed: a model that has not run for a while reads as having consumed little, so an ask that arrives for it is not made to wait behind a long run on the other
  def qsr-eff(c, now) = record_get(c[22], "gpu_ms") / (1 + (now - record_get(c[22], "gpu_at")) / 8000);
  def qsr-pick(ms, Ss) {
   let now = host_monotonic_ms();
   foldl((best, i) => svs-idle?(Ss[i]) ? best : (best < 0 || qsr-eff(ms[i][0], now) < qsr-eff(ms[best][0], now) ? i : best), -1, range(0, len(ms)));
  }
  def qsr-tick(ms, Ss, i) {
   let c = ms[i][0];
   let t0 = host_monotonic_ms();
   let counted = record_set(c[22], "ticks", record_get(c[22], "ticks") + 1);
   let r = try svs-tick(Ss[i], ms[i][1]) catch nothing();
   nothing?(r) ? qsr-abort(ms, Ss, "the pass raised (a surprise in the step of " ++ c[23] ++ ")") : qsr-after(ms, svs-put(Ss, i, r[0]), c, r[1], t0);
  }
  def qsr-after(ms, Ss, c, fin, t0) {
   let wrote = qsr-finish(c, fin);
   let now = host_monotonic_ms();
   let billed = record_set(c[22], "gpu_ms", qsr-eff(c, t0) + (now - t0));
   let at = record_set(c[22], "gpu_at", now);
   let eased = qsr-evict(c);
   let beat = foldl((n, j) => n + qsr-beat(ms[j][0], Ss[j]), 0, range(0, len(ms)));
   qsr-loop(ms, Ss, 0);
  }
  // nothing runs on any model
  def qsr-quiet(ms, Ss, stopping, idle_since) {
   let beat = foldl((n, j) => n + qsr-beat(ms[j][0], Ss[j]) + qsr-evict(ms[j][0]), 0, range(0, len(ms)));
   let now = host_monotonic_ms();
   let since = idle_since == 0 ? now : idle_since;
   let limit_ms = qsr-int(ms[0][0][10], "idle_exit_ms", 0);
   stopping ? "a stop file was found and nothing runs" : limit_ms > 0 && now - since > limit_ms ? "idle for " ++ limit_ms.str() ++ " ms" : qsr-nap(ms, Ss, since);
  }
  def qsr-nap(ms, Ss, since) {
   // an idle server rests on the request bell's seq word (a client rings it after it renames a request into req/): the kernel ends the rest at the ring;
   // the cap only covers a client that rang nothing
   let c = ms[0][0];
   let slept = nothing?(record_get(SV, "bell")) ? host_sleep_ms(qsr-clamp(qsr-int(c[10], "poll_ms", 20), 1, 5000)) : host_sleep_ms([qsr-clamp(qsr-int(c[10], "poll_ms", 20) * 50, 1000, 5000), record_get(SV, "bell")]);
   qsr-loop(ms, Ss, since);
  }
  // a step that raised: every sequence it held is answered by name and the server ends (the lease goes back with the door)
  def qsr-abort(ms, Ss, why) {
   let t = host_monotonic_ms();
   let wrote = foldl((n, i) => n + qsr-finish(ms[i][0], map(s => svs-finish(s, "server-error", t), append(append(Ss[i][0], Ss[i][2]), Ss[i][1]))), 0, range(0, len(ms)));
   why;
  }
  // ── the spool ──
  def qsr-intake(ms, Ss) {
   let names = filter(n => qsr-suffix?(n, ".json"), host_dir_list(ms[0][0][7] ++ "/req") ?? []);
   foldl((acc, n) => qsr-claim(ms, acc, n), Ss, names);
  }
  def qsr-claim(ms, Ss, name) {
   let dir = ms[0][0][7];
   let id = substring(name, 0, len(name) - 5);
   let moved = host_path_rename(dir ++ "/req/" ++ name, dir ++ "/work/" ++ name);
   moved != 0 ? Ss : qsr-read(ms, Ss, id, host_monotonic_ms());
  }
  // A request's id begins with its client's pid. A client that is gone will never read the reply, so its request is not generated: a crashed flow used to leave
  // its asks in the queue and the GPU spent minutes on answers no one took. Checked when a request is claimed and, once in two seconds, over every phase.
  def qsr-owner-gone?(id) {
   let d = str_find(id, "-", 0);
   let pid = d < 1 ? 0 : (try str_to_int(substring(id, 0, d)) catch 0);
   pid > 0 && (String) value_kind(host_process(pid)) != "list";
  }
  // Every phase is checked (queued, the ones prefilling, decoding): the scheduler ends a gone client's sequence and gives its blocks back,
  // and the server answers it like any end (a reply no one reads, a ledger row naming "owner-gone", the work file removed).
  def qsr-shed-all(ms, Ss) = map(i => qsr-shed(ms[i][0], ms[i][1], Ss[i]), range(0, len(ms)));
  def qsr-shed(c, env, S) {
   let now = host_monotonic_ms();
   now - record_get(c[22], "shed_at") < 2000 ? S : qsr-shed-go(c, env, S, now);
  }
  def qsr-shed-go(c, env, S, now) {
   let a = record_set(c[22], "shed_at", now);
   let r = svs-shed(S, env, id => qsr-owner-gone?(id));
   let w = qsr-finish(c, r[1]);
   let sg = foldl((n, s) => n + qsr-orphaned(s[0]), 0, r[1]);
   let fr = foldl((n, s) => n + qsr-pre-free(s[0]), 0, r[1]);
   r[0];
  }
  def qsr-orphaned(id) {
   let sg = qsr-sig("disc", 0, 1, "owner-gone", id, 0);
   0;
  }
  def qsr-read(ms, Ss, id, arrive) {
   let dir = ms[0][0][7];
   let text = read_file(dir ++ "/work/" ++ id ++ ".json");
   let p = svs-parse(id, nothing?(text) ? "" : text);
   qsr-owner-gone?(id) ? qsr-orphan-claim(Ss, id) : (String) p[0] == "ok" ? qsr-routed(ms, Ss, id, arrive, p[1]) : qsr-refuse(dir, Ss, id, p[1]);
  }
  def qsr-orphan-claim(Ss, id) {
   let a = qsr-orphaned(id);
   Ss;
  }
  def qsr-refuse(dir, Ss, id, why) {
   let row = svs-refused-row(id, why, now_unix_ms());
   let a = qsr-put(dir, dir ++ "/reply/" ++ id ++ ".json", row ++ "\n");
   let b = qsr-append(dir ++ "/ledger.jsonl", row ++ "\n");
   let d = host_path_remove(dir ++ "/work/" ++ id ++ ".json");
   let said = qsr-say("refused " ++ id ++ ": " ++ why);
   Ss;
  }
  // a request goes to the model it names, else to the registry's first held voice for its role (its `who`), else to the first model; a named model that is not held is refused by name
  def qsr-index-of(ms, name) = foldl((f, i) => f < 0 && (String) ms[i][0][23] == name ? i : f, -1, range(0, len(ms)));
  def qsr-route(ms, r) = len(r[11]) > 0 ? qsr-index-of(ms, r[11]) : qsr-role-index(ms, svs-role-of(r[7]));
  def qsr-role-index(ms, role) {
   let i = foldl((f, n) => f >= 0 ? f : qsr-index-of(ms, n), -1, mr-chain-names(role));
   i < 0 ? 0 : i;
  }
  def qsr-routed(ms, Ss, id, arrive, r) {
   let i = qsr-route(ms, r);
   i < 0 ? qsr-refuse(ms[0][0][7], Ss, id, "model-not-loaded: " ++ r[11] ++ " (held: " ++ qsr-list(map(m => m[0][23], ms)) ++ ")") : svs-put(Ss, i, qsr-take(ms[i][0], Ss[i], id, arrive, r));
  }
  // a chat request is the user turn (the question) and then the turn's own end (the lens text, the assistant's opening): its question ends at `boundary` ids, where a snapshot is kept
  def qsr-ids-at(c, r, pre) = r[3] == 1 ? append(pre, qlz-chat-lens(c[0], r[2], "")) : qlz-tokenize(c[0], r[1]);
  def qsr-insert(x, xs) = nil?(xs) ? [x] : x == xs[0] ? xs : x < xs[0] ? cons(x, xs) : cons(xs[0], qsr-insert(x, xs[1:]));
  // the snapshot positions of a sequence of n ids (the lane reads n - 1): the question's end, and 1024, 2048, 4096 ... ids; each strictly inside what the lane reads
  def qsr-doubles(p, n) = p >= n - 1 ? [] : cons(p, qsr-doubles(p * 2, n));
  def qsr-points(boundary, n) = foldl((acc, p) => p > 0 && p < n - 1 ? qsr-insert(p, acc) : acc, [], cons(boundary, qsr-doubles(1024, n)));
  def qsr-take(c, S, id, arrive, r) {
   let t0 = host_monotonic_ms();
   let pre = r[3] == 1 ? qlz-chat-prefix(c[0], r[1]) : [];
   let ids = qsr-ids-at(c, r, pre);
   let seq = svs-put(svs-with-points(svs-seq(r, ids, arrive), qsr-points(len(pre), len(ids))), 32, c[23]);
   let sg = qsr-sig("ok", len(ids), 0, "claimed", id, host_monotonic_ms() - t0);
   let said = qsr-say("claimed " ++ id ++ " for " ++ c[23] ++ " (" ++ r[7] ++ ", priority " ++ r[6].str() ++ "): " ++ len(ids).str() ++ " prompt ids, tokenized in " ++ (host_monotonic_ms() - t0).str() ++ " ms");
   svs-submit(S, seq);
  }
  // each finished sequence: its reply file (whole or absent), its ledger row, its work file gone
  def qsr-finish(c, fin) = foldl((n, s) => n + qsr-done(c, s), 0, fin);
  // every ask the server answers also lands one row in the machine's local-run ledger (receipts/local-run-ledger.jsonl), where the planner's read-time model and the rate
  // readings look: the ids the lane READ this time (the prompt less what the prefix cache already held, so a cached prompt never reads as a fast prefill) and the ms it took
  def qsr-local-run(c, s, text) {
   let status = (String) s[15] == "refused" || (String) s[15] == "server-error" || (String) s[15] == "empty-prompt" || (String) s[15] == "pool-too-small" || (String) s[15] == "pool-full" || (String) s[15] == "owner-gone" ? "unavailable" : "answered";
   let result = [status, text, len(s[3]) - s[21], s[17], c[24], 1, 1, status == "answered" ? "" : "serve-" ++ s[15], "", [], ""];
   // a read of fewer than 16 ids is all fixed cost (the copy of a cached state, the first chunk's launch): no prefill rate is stated for it
   local-run-record-timed(result, s[19] - s[2], len(s[3]) - s[21] < 16 ? 0 : s[16], svs-decode-ms(s));
  }
  def qsr-done(c, s) {
   let text = svs-trim-stop(qlz-detok(c[0], svs-gen(s)), s[5]);
   let at = now_unix_ms();
   let a = qsr-put(c[7], c[7] ++ "/reply/" ++ s[0] ++ ".json", svs-reply-row(s, text, at) ++ "\n");
   let b = qsr-append(c[7] ++ "/ledger.jsonl", svs-ledger-row(s, at) ++ "\n");
   let g = qsr-local-run(c, s, text);
   let d = host_path_remove(c[7] ++ "/work/" ++ s[0] ++ ".json");
   let e = record_set(SV, "served", record_get(SV, "served") + 1);
   let sg = qsr-sig("ok", s[17], len(s[3]), "done-" ++ s[15], s[0], s[12] - s[2]);
   let f = record_set(SV, "tokens", record_get(SV, "tokens") + s[17]);
   let said = qsr-say("done " ++ s[0] ++ " " ++ c[23] ++ " " ++ s[15] ++ " prompt_ids=" ++ len(s[3]).str() ++ " generated_ids=" ++ s[17].str() ++ " queue_ms=" ++ (s[12] - s[2]).str() ++ " prefill_ms=" ++ s[16].str() ++ " decode_tok_s=" ++ svs-tenths(svs-tok-s10(s)));
   1;
  }
  // the status the clients read, written at opening and when the models stand (the live reading is the signal frame and the log)
  def qsr-status(dir, state, start, label, S, pool) = qsr-put(dir, dir ++ "/status.json", svs-status-row(S, host_pid(), start, label ++ " " ++ state, now_unix_ms(), nothing?(pool) ? 0 : svb-used(pool), nothing?(pool) ? 0 : svb-capacity(pool), nothing?(pool) ? 0 : svb-bsz(pool)) ++ "\n");
  def qsr-beat(c, S) {
   let now = host_monotonic_ms();
   now - record_get(c[22], "beat_at") < 1000 ? 0 : qsr-beat-write(c, S, now);
  }
  // The beat is a cell in the signal frame (flow-signal.bml, /fgn-flow-15), given when the live, queued or pool reading moved: nothing is written to
  // the disk per beat (status.json names the server once, at opening, for the clients that look for one standing)
  def qsr-sig(kind, got, missed, why, ids, ms) = nothing?(record_get(SV, "flow")) ? 0 : fsg-emit(record_get(SV, "flow"), "serve", kind, got, missed, why, ids, ms);
  def qsr-beat-write(c, S, now) {
   let M = c[22];
   let key = svs-live(S).str() ++ "/" ++ svs-queued(S).str() ++ "/" ++ svb-used(c[15]).str();
   let w = key == record_get(M, "beat_key") ? 0 : qsr-sig("ok", svs-live(S), svs-queued(S), "beat", c[23] ++ " blocks=" ++ svb-used(c[15]).str() ++ "/" ++ svb-capacity(c[15]).str(), 0);
   let k = record_set(M, "beat_key", key);
   let a = record_set(M, "beat_at", now);
   let said = now - record_get(M, "beat_say") > 10000 && !svs-idle?(S) ? qsr-said-live(c, S, now) : 0;
   1;
  }
  def qsr-said-live(c, S, now) {
   let M = c[22];
   let steps = record_get(M, "steps");
   let said = qsr-say(c[23] ++ ": pool " ++ svb-used(c[15]).str() ++ " of " ++ svb-capacity(c[15]).str() ++ " blocks in use, " ++ len(record_get(M, "cache")).str() ++ " cached prefixes" ++ "; live " ++ svs-live(S).str() ++ " queued " ++ svs-queued(S).str() ++ " prefilling " ++ len(S[1]).str() ++ "; since the last line " ++ (now - record_get(M, "beat_say")).str() ++ " ms, " ++ record_get(M, "ticks").str() ++ " ticks, " ++ steps.str() ++ " decode steps averaging " ++ (steps > 0 ? record_get(M, "step_ms") / steps : 0).str() ++ " ms");
   let a = record_set(M, "beat_say", now);
   let b = record_set(M, "step_ms", 0);
   let d = record_set(M, "steps", 0);
   record_set(M, "ticks", 0);
  }
 }
 qsr-run();
}
